class.description:
A trait is declared with the [code]trait[/code] keyword and holds any member a class can hold, except inner classes. Classes bring a trait's members into themselves with [code]uses[/code]. [codeblock] class_name Player extends Node uses Damageable, Movable
func take_damage(amount: int) -> void: # Overrides the trait's implementation. health -= amount if health <= 0: died.emit()
func _physics_process(delta: float) -> void: move(Vector2.RIGHT) [/codeblock] A trait is not a base type: it cannot be instantiated, and it cannot be inherited from with [code]extends[/code]. Its members are copied into every class that uses it, which is what makes a trait's state per-instance rather than shared. [b]Note:[/b] Traits can only be declared and used within the same script file. Referencing a trait from another file is not supported yet.
